{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an automated orchestrator) requested implementation of `cmd/pathchk/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. This is stitch task #5598 from generation run 44. The task covers SRD103 requirements R1.1 through R1.4 - implementing the core pathname validation logic for the `pathchk` utility, which checks whether file names are valid or portable according to POSIX rules. The utility must match GNU `gpathchk` behavior. The task explicitly scopes only file creation (`cmd/pathchk/main.go`) and requires compilation verification via `go build` and `go vet`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU pathchk validates pathnames against POSIX portability rules\n   - Three validation modes: default (system validity check), `-p`/`--portability` (strict POSIX portable chars, 14-char component limit, 256-char path limit), `-P` (no leading hyphens in components)\n   - POSIX portable filename characters: A-Z, a-z, 0-9, period, underscore, hyphen\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing pattern against `gpathchk` reference binary\n   - Errors reported to stderr; exit 0 if all paths valid, exit 1 if any invalid\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines hard limit\n   - File size limit: 500 lines\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd103-pathchk.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining all requirements for pathchk\n     - R1.1: Check pathnames for validity on current system (component too long, non-existent leading directory)\n     - R1.2: `-p`/`--portability` checks: only portable chars (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, ., _, -), component ≤14 chars, total path ≤256 chars\n     - R1.3: `-P` checks: no leading hyphen in any component\n     - R1.4: Process multiple pathname arguments, checking each\n     - R2.1: Exit 0 when all pass; R2.2: Exit 1 when any fail; R2.3: SIGPIPE via InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n     - Non-goals: does not create or modify files\n     - Package contract imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED in project_context)\n     - Shows the InstallSIGPIPEHandler pattern used by all cmd/ utilities\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/pathchk/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Must implement all R1.1-R1.4 requirements\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n     - Import: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - implementation has not started. The SRD was read successfully.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand requirements before implementing\n   - No implementation work has been done yet - was about to begin writing code\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task prompt containing all project context, SRDs, architecture, execution constitution, go style constitution, task description, constraints, and requirements for implementing cmd/pathchk (srd103 R1.1-R1.4)\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting this summary\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/pathchk/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4 of srd103-pathchk\n   - Verify compilation with `go build -o bin/pathchk ./cmd/pathchk/`\n   - Verify with `go vet ./cmd/pathchk/`\n   - Ensure all acceptance criteria AC1-AC4 are met\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd103-pathchk.yaml`) and was about to implement `cmd/pathchk/main.go`. No code has been written yet. The implementation needs to:\n   - Parse `-p`/`--portability` and `-P` flags\n   - For default mode (no flags): check each pathname component exists and isn't too long for the current system\n   - For `-p` mode: validate chars are in portable set (A-Za-z0-9._-), components ≤14 chars, total path ≤256 chars\n   - For `-P` mode: check no component starts with a hyphen\n   - Process multiple pathname arguments (R1.4)\n   - Print errors to stderr, exit 0 if all valid, exit 1 if any invalid\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/pathchk/main.go` implementing all R1.1-R1.4 requirements, then verify with `go build -o bin/pathchk ./cmd/pathchk/` and `go vet ./cmd/pathchk/`. The task description states: \"Implement srd103-pathchk R1.1 through R1.4 as specified in the SRD\" with design decision D1: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project SIGPIPE protocol\" and acceptance criteria AC1: \"cmd/pathchk/main.go exists and compiles with go build ./cmd/pathchk/\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5598/e97c73f4-4027-474d-b337-bb9a89ad4527.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e97c73f4-4027-474d-b337-bb9a89ad4527","uuid":"f33a5e03-7b5c-403f-b7a0-f95d068dd7e3","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:33:16.693Z","isSynthetic":true}
