{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ab8b5eb6ceae68287","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxWPahfEDXRg9WhSaGA74R","status":"completed","output_file":"","summary":"Explore existing cmd/ patterns","usage":{"total_tokens":37333,"tool_uses":12,"duration_ms":45351},"uuid":"2b232173-1d3d-4cf2-840d-5f981be7bfab","session_id":"e97c73f4-4027-474d-b337-bb9a89ad4527"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxWPahfEDXRg9WhSaGA74R","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Report: Go Project Coding Patterns\n\n### 1. **Flag Parsing Pattern**\n\nThe project uses **manual flag parsing with string-based switch statements** (no external CLI framework like cobra in these cmd/ utilities):\n\n- **Flag structure**: Functions named `parseArgs()` that accept `[]string` arguments\n- **Long flags**: Checked with `strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\")`, then matched in a switch\n- **Short flags**: Short flag letters extracted with `arg[1:]`, processed in separate `parseShortFlags()` functions\n- **Flag terminator**: `--` stops flag parsing; remaining args are operands\n- **Help/Version**: Early exit with `os.Exit(0)` when `--help` or `--version` encountered\n- **Invalid flags**: Errors printed to stderr, exit code 1 or 2\n\n**Example from tty/main.go (lines 56-103)**:\n```go\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) bool {\n  for _, arg := range args {\n    switch {\n    case arg == \"--help\":\n      fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n      os.Exit(0)\n    case strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\"):\n      fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tty: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", arg)\n      fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'tty --help' for more information.\")\n      os.Exit(2)\n    case strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") && len(arg) > 1:\n      silent = parseShortFlags(arg[1:], silent)\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. **Error Output Pattern**\n\nErrors follow a consistent format:\n\n- **Stderr output format**: `<progname>: <error message>`\n- **Use of `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...)`** for error messages\n- **Help text on error**: `fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try '<cmd> --help' for more information.\")`\n- **No error wrapping in cmd/**: Errors are printed directly in main, not bubbled up\n- **Error details**: Include the problematic operand or option in the message\n\n**Example from basename/main.go (lines 45-50)**:\n```go\nopts, names, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\nif err != nil {\n  fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"basename: %s\\n\", err)\n  fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'basename --help' for more information.\\n\")\n  os.Exit(1)\n}\n```\n\n### 3. **Exit Code Pattern**\n\nExit codes are explicitly controlled with `os.Exit()`:\n\n- **0**: Successful execution or when help/version is printed\n- **1**: General errors (missing operand, bad argument, runtime failure)\n- **2**: Invalid option/flag syntax (unrecognized flag, missing arg)\n- **Print I/O errors**: When `fmt.Fprintln()` to stdout fails, exit 1 immediately\n\n**From pathchk/main.go (lines 44-61)**:\n```go\ncode := 0\nfor _, name := range names {\n  if !checkPath(name, opts) {\n    code = 1  // Accumulate failures\n  }\n}\nos.Exit(code)\n```\n\n### 4. **SIGPIPE Handler Usage**\n\nEvery main.go calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` as the **first line in main()**:\n\n- **Import path**: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n- **Function signature**: `func InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` (no parameters)\n- **Behavior**: Exits with code 0 when stdout/stderr is closed downstream\n- **Purpose**: Matches GNU coreutils behavior when piped to a command that closes early\n\n**From all cmd/*/main.go files (line 31-32)**:\n```go\nfunc main() {\n  sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n  // ... rest of logic\n}\n```\n\n### 5. **Style Constraints from go-style.yaml**\n\nKey constraints that apply to your work:\n\n1. **Function size limit**: **200 lines max** (go-style.yaml line 371)\n   - \"No function exceeds 200 lines without a strong reason.\"\n   - If a function approaches 200 lines, find a seam and split it into helpers\n\n2. **Parameter limit**: **3 parameters max** (go-style.yaml line 137)\n   - Group related parameters into a config struct if exceeding 3\n\n3. **Struct responsibility**: Each struct represents **one concept**\n\n4. **Error handling**: Use guard clauses, wrap with `fmt.Errorf(\"context: %w\", err)`\n\n5. **Copyright header**: Every .go file starts with:\n   ```go\n   // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n   // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n   ```\n\n6. **Implementation strategy**: Write all files before running build/test (no incremental compile-fix loops)\n\n7. **Comment style**: Exported symbols must have godoc comments starting with the symbol name\n\n### 6. **cmd/pathchk/ Directory Contents**\n\nThe directory exists with:\n- `main.go` (5972 bytes) - Full implementation with flag parsing, POSIX/portability checks\n- `pathchk_test.go` (3259 bytes) - Test file\n\nPathchk implements detailed path validation with multiple check modes (-p for POSIX, -P for leading hyphen, --portability for both).\n\n---\n\n**Absolute file paths for reference**:\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5598/cmd/tty/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5598/cmd/pwd/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5598/cmd/basename/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5598/cmd/pathchk/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5598/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5598/docs/constitutions/go-style.yaml`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e97c73f4-4027-474d-b337-bb9a89ad4527","uuid":"c6f2ae07-0ea9-4d5e-8a49-5c9fe47461a5","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:34:11.851Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the coding patterns used in this Go project's cmd/ utilities. \n\n1. Find a few existing cmd/*/main.go files and read them to understand the style: flag parsing, error handling, exit codes, stderr output, SIGPIPE handler usage. Pick 2-3 simple utilities.\n2. Check if cmd/pathchk/ directory